  "raw_text": "Step 1: Alice wins immediately if she gets heads on her first turn. The probability of this happening is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n\nStep 2: If Alice does not get heads (probability \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\)), then it becomes Bob's turn. Bob wins if he gets tails, which has a probability of \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\). If Bob does not get tails (probability \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\)), the game returns to Alice.\n\nStep 3: If the game returns to Alice, we can consider this as a new round starting from Alice's turn again. The probability that Alice wins from this point onward is the same as the original probability we are trying to find.\n\nStep 4: Let \\( P \\) be the probability that Alice wins the game. We can set up the equation based on the above reasoning:\n\\[ P = \\frac{1}{2} + \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times P \\right) \\]\nThis equation accounts for Alice winning immediately or the game returning to Alice after both fail to win on their respective turns.\n\nStep 5: Simplify the equation:\n\\[ P = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4}P \\]\n\nStep 6: Solve for \\( P \\):\n\\[ P - \\frac{1}{4}P = \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{3}{4}P = \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\\[ P = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n\\[ P = \\frac{2}{3} \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\frac{2}{3}}<|im_end|>",
  "reforward_peak_bytes": 15471579136,
